                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_210\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes a single line in FlexReader.java's file-grouping loop:\n\n    file.field = field % runCount;\n  ->\n    file.field = field % (nFiles / (wellCount * runCount));\n\nThis shows the bug was an incorrect field-index computation (\"field % runCount\") used when assigning FlexFile.field for each file, which produced wrong field indices whenever multiple acquisition \"runs\" were present (causing incorrect file indexing/lookup for wells with more than one run).\n\nTracing the history of this exact line across the candidates:\n- candidate_202 is where multi-run support (runCount, runDirs, acquisition tracking) was first introduced. At that point the line read:\n      file.field = field / runCount;\n  (division, not modulo) \u2014 this was the original multi-run-aware computation.\n- candidate_210 changed this same line from division to modulo:\n      file.field = field / runCount;   ->   file.field = field % runCount;\n  This is exactly the buggy expression (\"field % runCount\") that the fix commit later replaces. No candidate between 210 and the fix touches this line again.\n- The fix commit (and the near-identical diff seen in candidate_211, which appears to correspond to the fix itself rather than a bug-introducing change) corrects the formula to \"field % (nFiles / (wellCount * runCount))\".\n\nSince candidate_210 is the commit that introduced the precise faulty expression (\"field % runCount\") that persisted unchanged until the fix, it is the bug-introducing commit. candidate_202, while it added the multi-run feature and a related but different (division-based) computation, did not contain the specific buggy pattern that the fix directly addresses.\n"
                }
